# Dependencies — never commit these. Committing node_modules is what broke
# every Vercel production build from ~2026-08-14 to 2026-08-16: git stored
# node_modules/.bin/tsc with mode 100644 (non-executable), so the Linux build
# box hit "Permission denied" running `tsc -b` and exited 126. package-lock.json
# is committed instead, which reproduces the exact dependency tree on install.
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local tooling state
.vercel
supabase/.temp/

# Screenshots from `npm run render:screens` — a looking tool, not an artifact.
.screens/

# Diagnostic report artifacts — regenerated by the sweeps, never source.
# meal-quality-report.txt was never committed until it was swept in by a
# `git add -A` during a background run; PROJECT-LOG says to discard it after
# every run. The other two are TRACKED snapshots (a regeneration must not be
# committed, but the file itself stays), so they can't be listed here —
# .githooks/pre-commit refuses those instead.
meal-quality-report.txt
.tour-harness/dist/
.tour-harness/*.png
